      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Edit 6/20/2023 - 19:48 UTC\n\nWith some further testing, it seems that we do have access to setting the Fixed Timestep which does affect the FixedUpdate rate. However, this is immediately reset back to the normal VRC value and other Udon Behaviours may not see the change. We can set this every FixedUpdate to enforce it for our Udon Behaviour though this feels unintentional since other Udon Behaviours may not see the change and the VRC client \"fights\" to reset this back.\n\nThe ability to manually set our own Fixed Timestep would be a nice addition.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-06-15T21:41:52.990Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The normal unity method FixedUpdate changes on the VRChat client depending on the refresh rate of the monitor or max headset framerate. Which for some can be changed while playing VRChat!\n\nThis can be compensated by using Time.deltaTime in the right places, however, this is still inconsistent than having a constant update loop. It also complicates graph programming and code by adding or multiplying Time.deltaTime to everything.\n\nIt would be useful to have a built-in function that is called at a constant rate. ConstantFixedUpdate (or something named similarly) would be called at a constant rate for all devices. Maybe unity's default 20 calls per second or 60 calls per second, as long as it's constant and usable with controlling physics.\n\nThis would also help and ensure things are running at the same rate for all players in a world.",
